{"availability":"available","full":"owebeeone/grip-sudoku","name":"grip-sudoku","description":"Sudoku SPA built as a GRIP demo: no React state, everything is a grip","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-22T14:29:53Z","updated":"2026-09-22T14:39:24Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://owebeeone.github.io/grip-sudoku/","topics":["grip","react","reactjs"],"demo":"https://owebeeone.github.io/grip-sudoku/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:47.861Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:47.861Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:47.861Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:39:47.861Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A complete Sudoku single-page app — sign in, pick a difficulty, play with pen and pencil marks, undo/redo, a timer, mistake limits, auto-save, a dashboard with stats and leaderboards, and a profile with run history — built as a demonstration of GRIP (@owebeeone/grip-react).","The point of the demo: there is no React state in this app. Not one useState, useEffect, useRef, useReducer, useMemo, useCallback, or useLayoutEffect. Every value a component renders is read from a grip, and every change goes through a tap. That rule is enforced by a lint rule and an independent test (see Enforcement), so it can't quietly erode.","Sign in with demo@gripsudoku.app and any password. The backend is mocked — auth, stats, and leaderboards are fixture data served through taps with a simulated network delay, so the UI exercises real loading/async paths."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/owebeeone/grip-sudoku/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"aff859acc8b93f67ad665daa1e8d21ec24e591929b126a97c00f695f2bde8c1c","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:48.029Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:48.029Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A complete Sudoku single-page app — sign in, pick a difficulty, pla